          "title": "You'll want to know: das Referat",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "das Referat — \"the class talk, the oral report\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Morgen halte ich ein Referat über Wale. Tomorrow I am giving a talk in class about whales."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Referate. Ein Referat halten — to give a talk. In an office, das Referat is also a section."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Referat comes from the Latin verb form referat \"let him report\", from referre \"to carry back, to bring back word\" (Lewis & Short). It is usually said to have been first a note on a document, then the report itself."
            }
          ]
        },
